## Module 2: Set Theory, Relations, and Functions## Deep-Dive Implementation Manual
In secure software development and threat modeling, Set Theory is used to analyze access controls, data boundaries, and isolated execution privileges. When a developer makes an error in their structural boundaries, data leaks from private sets into public sets.
